WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:03.603
-The House took
a historic vote today

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:05.471
to endorse the impeachment
inquiry into President Trump

00:00:05.471 --> 00:00:07.573
and set out rules for
the next stage of the process.

00:00:07.573 --> 00:00:09.575
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:09.575 --> 00:00:13.546
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.546 --> 00:00:16.182
This was the first time
the full House voted

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:18.184
on the current impeachment
inquiry into Trump.

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:20.453
It's a day
that he has long dreaded,

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:23.356
and you can tell because the
further along impeachment got,

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:24.657
the more he started
to freak out.

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:27.694
-The President tweeted that the,
"Do-nothing Democrats

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:30.163
should be focused
on building up our country."

00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:32.732
He said, "Not wasting
everyone's time and energy

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:35.034
on," all-caps, "Bull [bleep]"

00:00:35.034 --> 00:00:39.338
-They can't win on election day,
so they're pursuing an illegal,

00:00:39.338 --> 00:00:45.211
invalid, and unconstitutional
bull [bleep] impeachment.

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:47.547
-The angrier Trump gets,
the more he sounds

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:50.316
like a cab driver from Queens.

00:00:50.316 --> 00:00:52.818
"You want me to take you to
LaGuardia at 4:00 p.m.?

00:00:52.818 --> 00:00:54.287
This is bull [bleep]

00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:55.388
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:58.491
Keep walking!

00:00:58.491 --> 00:01:00.493
Get an Uber!"

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:02.428
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:02.428 --> 00:01:03.896
Also, I like when you can tell

00:01:03.896 --> 00:01:06.098
which words
were written for Trump

00:01:06.098 --> 00:01:07.834
and which ones he added.

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:09.669
"All right, uh, Mr. President,
here's the script.

00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:12.405
We're gonna call it illegal,
invalid, and unconstitutional."

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:14.874
"Okay, yeah, that's good.
I might add one word."

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:16.042
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:17.710
"Is it a bad word?"
"No."

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:19.278
"Donald, if it's a bad word,

00:01:19.278 --> 00:01:20.913
you have to put a dollar
in the swear jar."

00:01:20.913 --> 00:01:22.548
"What?
I thought if I swear,

00:01:22.548 --> 00:01:25.418
I get to take a dollar
out of the swear jar.

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:28.054
This is bull [bleep]

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:29.756
That's one you owe me."

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:31.057
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.057 --> 00:01:33.025
So, Trump was clearly
dreading this vote, and yet,

00:01:33.025 --> 00:01:34.994
even as late as this morning,
his advisers were

00:01:34.994 --> 00:01:37.696
still insisting
that Democrats would fail.

00:01:37.696 --> 00:01:39.198
White House counselor
Kellyanne Conway

00:01:39.198 --> 00:01:41.267
went on Fox News
and claimed that she had

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:43.469
some inside dirt
on the impeachment process.

00:01:43.469 --> 00:01:45.204
-Impeachment is simple math.

00:01:45.204 --> 00:01:47.340
You either
have the votes or you don't.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.241
And guess what --
dirty little secret --

00:01:49.241 --> 00:01:50.643
they don't have the votes.

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:53.011
-Kellyanne Conway
definitely seems like someone

00:01:53.011 --> 00:01:55.481
who spent high school
sharing dirty little secrets.

00:01:55.481 --> 00:01:58.017
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.017 --> 00:02:00.353
She should be standing
by a locker, whispering,

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:02.288
"Jackie's boyfriend
told Jeff's sister

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:04.323
who told Dana's cousin
who told Mike's cousin

00:02:04.323 --> 00:02:06.659
who told Sophie's mom
who told Jason's mom,

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:08.961
who told Danny's prom date,
that -- guess what --

00:02:08.961 --> 00:02:10.330
they don't have the vote."

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:14.633
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.633 --> 00:02:17.269
But there you go --
Kellyanne Conway says Democrats

00:02:17.269 --> 00:02:19.738
don't have the votes to impeach
Trump, and if that's the case,

00:02:19.738 --> 00:02:21.474
then surely,
they wouldn't have the votes

00:02:21.474 --> 00:02:23.009
for today's resolution.

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:25.811
-A historic vote just held
in the House of Representatives.

00:02:25.811 --> 00:02:28.214
The Democratic-controlled
Congress voting to move ahead

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:30.416
with the impeachment inquiry.

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:32.818
-House Democrats
and one independent lawmaker

00:02:32.818 --> 00:02:35.588
passing a resolution laying out
the impeachment process

00:02:35.588 --> 00:02:37.323
by an overwhelming majority.

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:44.363
-On this vote, the yeas are 232,
the nays are 196.

00:02:44.363 --> 00:02:47.066
-What?
We can't trust Kellyanne Conway?

00:02:47.066 --> 00:02:48.368
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.368 --> 00:02:50.803
I guess up is up
and down is down.

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:52.371
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.371 --> 00:02:53.939
And for her part,
House Speaker Nancy Pelosi

00:02:53.939 --> 00:02:55.408
played it cool
and made clear the whole time

00:02:55.408 --> 00:02:56.709
she was confident
she had the votes.

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:58.845
In fact, right before
she presided over the vote,

00:02:58.845 --> 00:03:01.514
she spoke to reporters and at
the end of her press conference,

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:03.782
she coyly teased
what she was about to do.

00:03:03.782 --> 00:03:06.652
-As you may understand,
I have business on the floor

00:03:06.652 --> 00:03:08.921
that I have to see to,
so I'm going to excuse myself.

00:03:08.921 --> 00:03:10.256
Thank you all very much.

00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:12.891
-Damn!
That's like in an action movie

00:03:12.891 --> 00:03:16.195
when Tom Cruise says something
like, "Sorry. This is my stop,"

00:03:16.195 --> 00:03:18.164
and then jumps out
of an airplane.

00:03:18.164 --> 00:03:19.966
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.966 --> 00:03:21.700
And while Pelosi
was playing it cool,

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:23.603
Trump and his allies, of course,
were freaking out.

00:03:23.603 --> 00:03:27.206
In fact, Trump is so desperate
and so wildly grasping at straws

00:03:27.206 --> 00:03:29.175
that, this morning,
he just blurted out

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:31.443
an all-caps tweet
about his infamous phone call

00:03:31.443 --> 00:03:33.512
with the president of Ukraine
that just said,

00:03:33.512 --> 00:03:35.281
"Read the transcript."

00:03:35.281 --> 00:03:36.648
Yeah, we did.

00:03:36.648 --> 00:03:40.553
That's how we found out about
the crimes you committed.

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:43.389
Trump's like a bank robber
who screams, "Watch the tape!"

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:47.059
Then the jury watches the tape,
and it's just him smiling

00:03:47.059 --> 00:03:49.328
straight in the camera,
holding up a bag of cash.

00:03:49.328 --> 00:03:52.098
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:52.098 --> 00:03:55.368
Then...

00:03:55.368 --> 00:03:57.169
later in the morning,
Trump tweeted again,

00:03:57.169 --> 00:03:58.470
this time even more desperate

00:03:58.470 --> 00:04:00.105
and trying out
an even dumber argument.

00:04:00.105 --> 00:04:01.774
He tweeted,
"The impeachment hoax

00:04:01.774 --> 00:04:02.909
is hurting our stock market.

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:04.577
The do-nothing Democrats
don't care."

00:04:04.577 --> 00:04:06.245
That has nothing to do
with impeachment.

00:04:06.245 --> 00:04:09.047
There's no secret footnote
in the Constitution that says,

00:04:09.047 --> 00:04:11.551
"The president shall be removed
from office for treason,

00:04:11.551 --> 00:04:14.020
bribery, or other high crimes
and misdemeanors

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:15.287
unless it's bad
for the stock market,

00:04:15.287 --> 00:04:16.289
in which case, cool it."

00:04:16.289 --> 00:04:18.024
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.024 --> 00:04:20.126
And Trump
was not the only one at a loss

00:04:20.126 --> 00:04:21.927
for how to respond
to the impeachment vote today.

00:04:21.927 --> 00:04:24.863
Take Republican Congressman
Devin Nunes who complained about

00:04:24.863 --> 00:04:25.999
all the damning testimony

00:04:25.999 --> 00:04:27.500
Democrats have heard
from witnesses.

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:29.502
Democrats have been holding
those depositions

00:04:29.502 --> 00:04:32.371
in a secure room at the Capitol
known as the SCIF,

00:04:32.371 --> 00:04:34.607
and Nunes called
those hearings a cult.

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:36.542
-What we're seeing
among Democrats

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:39.678
on the intelligence committees
down in the SCIF right now

00:04:39.678 --> 00:04:41.614
is like a cult.

00:04:41.614 --> 00:04:44.850
These are a group of people
loyally following their leader

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:48.488
as he bounces from one
outlandish conspiracy theory

00:04:48.488 --> 00:04:49.755
to another.

00:04:49.755 --> 00:04:51.490
-You're calling Democrats
a cult?

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:52.992
Donald Trump
looks like something

00:04:52.992 --> 00:04:54.327
that was summoned by a cult.

00:04:54.327 --> 00:04:55.361
[ Laughter ]

00:04:55.361 --> 00:04:57.029
In fact,
Trump wasn't actually born.

00:04:57.029 --> 00:04:59.365
He just appeared one day
in the middle of a pentagram.

00:04:59.365 --> 00:05:00.399
[ Laughter ]

00:05:00.399 --> 00:05:02.969
-"Who has summoned me?

00:05:02.969 --> 00:05:04.837
And was she hot?
Was she like a 10?"

00:05:04.837 --> 00:05:06.238
[ Laughter ]

00:05:06.238 --> 00:05:08.374
"I don't like being summoned
by anything less than a 10.

00:05:08.374 --> 00:05:09.876
I'll go back to hell right now."

00:05:09.876 --> 00:05:11.343
[ Laughter ]

00:05:11.343 --> 00:05:13.412
And that wasn't even the dumbest
thing Republicans said

00:05:13.412 --> 00:05:15.048
before the vote,
because, as always,

00:05:15.048 --> 00:05:16.716
they also had dumb posters.

00:05:16.716 --> 00:05:18.584
Congressman Steve Scalise,
for example,

00:05:18.584 --> 00:05:20.953
brought out a giant poster
to accuse the Democrats

00:05:20.953 --> 00:05:23.355
of acting like Soviets
for following a procedure

00:05:23.355 --> 00:05:25.624
laid out by the founders
in the Constitution.

00:05:25.624 --> 00:05:27.026
-This is unprecedented.

00:05:27.026 --> 00:05:31.797
It's not only unprecedented,
this is Soviet-style rules.

00:05:31.797 --> 00:05:34.700
Maybe in the Soviet Union
you do things like this

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:36.535
where only you make the rules.

00:05:36.535 --> 00:05:38.670
Madam Speaker, when you look
through this resolution

00:05:38.670 --> 00:05:40.272
and you see how one-sided,

00:05:40.272 --> 00:05:42.541
how Soviet-style
this is running...

00:05:42.541 --> 00:05:44.410
-It looks like the cover
of a board game.

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:46.579
[ Laughter ]

00:05:46.579 --> 00:05:48.948
I feel so bad for the intern
who had to run to Kinkos

00:05:48.948 --> 00:05:50.015
and print that out.

00:05:50.015 --> 00:05:52.051
Look how janky that thing is.

00:05:52.051 --> 00:05:53.352
How did that conversation go?

00:05:53.352 --> 00:05:55.221
"Hey, I need a giant posterboard
of this."

00:05:55.221 --> 00:05:57.189
"Oh, is it for your child's
history class?"

00:05:57.189 --> 00:05:58.958
"No."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:58.958 --> 00:06:00.660
"It's more my Congressman."

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:01.894
[ Laughter ]

00:06:01.894 --> 00:06:04.396
But at least that guy
brought a visual aid.

00:06:04.396 --> 00:06:06.532
Republican Minority Leader
Kevin McCarthy

00:06:06.532 --> 00:06:09.001
tried to use his words,
but he said something

00:06:09.001 --> 00:06:12.070
so confusing that it was nearly
impossible to follow his logic.

00:06:12.070 --> 00:06:15.475
-This is the moment
that history will write.

00:06:15.475 --> 00:06:19.344
History will ask you,
when you cast this vote,

00:06:19.344 --> 00:06:22.147
when you cast a vote
to justify something

00:06:22.147 --> 00:06:25.917
that has gone on
behind closed doors...

00:06:25.917 --> 00:06:30.956
I want you to ask the historian
and answer the question.

00:06:30.956 --> 00:06:33.292
What do you know
that happened there?

00:06:33.292 --> 00:06:36.161
-What?
[ Laughter ]

00:06:36.161 --> 00:06:38.764
What are you saying?

00:06:38.764 --> 00:06:42.201
History will write this moment,
and then, history will ask you

00:06:42.201 --> 00:06:46.405
a question, so you want them
to ask the historian a question

00:06:46.405 --> 00:06:49.609
and then answer
the questions themselves?

00:06:49.609 --> 00:06:51.377
[ Laughter ]

00:06:51.377 --> 00:06:53.379
Sounds like you asked Siri
to read a quote

00:06:53.379 --> 00:06:56.749
from Alexander Hamilton after
spilling water on your phone.

00:06:56.749 --> 00:06:58.050
[ Laughter ]

00:06:58.050 --> 00:07:01.154
"Siri, read me a passage
from the "Federalist Papers."

00:07:01.154 --> 00:07:04.523
-History will write this moment,
and then, history will ask you

00:07:04.523 --> 00:07:07.994
a question and then you should
ask the historian a question,

00:07:07.994 --> 00:07:10.162
and then a historian
will answer it.

00:07:10.162 --> 00:07:12.999
[ Laughter ]

00:07:12.999 --> 00:07:14.867
-Today's vote was obviously
a historic moment

00:07:14.867 --> 00:07:16.535
and a huge blow to Trump
and his supporters.

00:07:16.535 --> 00:07:19.138
The House has now formally
endorsed the impeachment inquiry

00:07:19.138 --> 00:07:20.840
and that's because
the basic facts

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:22.140
of what happened
are indisputable.

00:07:22.140 --> 00:07:23.943
Trump orchestrated
a vast scheme in which

00:07:23.943 --> 00:07:26.345
he dangled hundreds of millions
of dollars in military aid

00:07:26.345 --> 00:07:29.181
to Ukraine in order to get
that country to dig up dirt

00:07:29.181 --> 00:07:31.183
on his political rivals,
and key witnesses

00:07:31.183 --> 00:07:33.786
over the last few weeks
have confirmed key details

00:07:33.786 --> 00:07:35.788
of what happened,
including new testimony today

00:07:35.788 --> 00:07:37.389
from a top
national-security official,

00:07:37.389 --> 00:07:40.459
and now Democrats
are planning on calling Trump's

00:07:40.459 --> 00:07:42.194
ex-national security adviser
John Bolton

00:07:42.194 --> 00:07:43.528
to testify in a few weeks.

00:07:43.528 --> 00:07:45.864
Now, you might remember
that when Bolton found out about

00:07:45.864 --> 00:07:48.334
the Ukraine quid pro quo
led by Trump's personal lawyer

00:07:48.334 --> 00:07:51.103
Rudy Giuliani, Bolton reportedly
told people at the White House,

00:07:51.103 --> 00:07:54.373
"Giuliani's a hand grenade who's
going to blow everybody up.

00:07:54.373 --> 00:07:55.674
Rudy's not a hand grenade.

00:07:55.674 --> 00:07:58.343
He's the guy who walks
into a room holding the pin.

00:07:58.343 --> 00:08:00.146
"Oh, Rudy, what'd you do?

00:08:00.146 --> 00:08:01.681
[ Laughter ]

00:08:01.681 --> 00:08:03.816
"You guys see
a little metal baseball?"

00:08:03.816 --> 00:08:06.018
[ Laughter ]

00:08:06.018 --> 00:08:09.488
So, Bolton wanted no part
of the Ukraine quid pro quo.

00:08:09.488 --> 00:08:11.858
In fact, you might also remember
that one of Trump's

00:08:11.858 --> 00:08:13.926
handpicked ambassadors,
Gordon Sondland,

00:08:13.926 --> 00:08:16.028
and his acting chief of staff
Mick Mulvaney,

00:08:16.028 --> 00:08:18.264
were both central in
orchestrating the quid pro quo

00:08:18.264 --> 00:08:20.699
with Ukraine, and when he found
out, Bolton reportedly said,

00:08:20.699 --> 00:08:22.902
"I'm not part of whatever
drug deal Sondland and Mulvaney

00:08:22.902 --> 00:08:26.038
are cooking up," and even if
you did want to be part of it,

00:08:26.038 --> 00:08:28.708
I'm not sure I'd trust these
guys to cook up a drug deal.

00:08:28.708 --> 00:08:30.943
They look like the only drugs
they've taken are the kinds

00:08:30.943 --> 00:08:32.678
you see in commercials
with middle-aged couples

00:08:32.678 --> 00:08:34.180
walking on beaches together.

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:36.047
[ Laughter ]

00:08:36.047 --> 00:08:38.317
If Mulvaney's called to testify
about his drug deal,

00:08:38.317 --> 00:08:40.786
the hearing will probably be
sponsored by one of those drugs.

00:08:40.786 --> 00:08:42.321
-Mr. Chairman, I thank you
for your time

00:08:42.321 --> 00:08:43.455
and for the opportunity
to be here.

00:08:43.455 --> 00:08:46.392
-♪ Viva Viagra ♪

00:08:46.392 --> 00:08:48.960
-So, Bolton obviously has a lot
to say, and on top of that,

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:51.831
he left the Trump administration
on very bad terms.

00:08:51.831 --> 00:08:54.400
Bolton, like almost every other
Trump aide before him,

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:57.736
was unceremoniously dumped last
month after clashing with Trump,

00:08:57.736 --> 00:08:59.772
and as usual,
Trump couldn't help

00:08:59.772 --> 00:09:01.607
but diss Bolton
on his way out the door.

00:09:01.607 --> 00:09:05.077
-He made some very big mistakes.

00:09:05.077 --> 00:09:06.678
You know,
John's known as a tough guy.

00:09:06.678 --> 00:09:09.248
He's so tough,
he got us into Iraq.

00:09:09.248 --> 00:09:10.382
That's tough.

00:09:10.382 --> 00:09:11.951
And, you know,
John wasn't in line

00:09:11.951 --> 00:09:14.787
with what we were doing,
and actually, in some cases,

00:09:14.787 --> 00:09:17.222
he thought it was too tough,
what we were doing.

00:09:17.222 --> 00:09:18.223
Mr. Tough Guy.

00:09:18.223 --> 00:09:20.225
You know,
you have to go into Iraq.

00:09:20.225 --> 00:09:21.961
Going into Iraq was something

00:09:21.961 --> 00:09:23.796
that he felt
very strongly about,

00:09:23.796 --> 00:09:26.465
and I disagreed with that
decision from the beginning.

00:09:26.465 --> 00:09:28.233
I thought
it was a terrible mistake.

00:09:28.233 --> 00:09:30.502
And that's not a question
of being tough.

00:09:30.502 --> 00:09:32.804
That's a question
of being not smart.

00:09:32.804 --> 00:09:34.840
So, I wish John the best.

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:37.476
-It doesn't sound like you do.

00:09:37.476 --> 00:09:40.212
You can't just end a long rant
about how he's an idiot

00:09:40.212 --> 00:09:42.581
by tacking on,
"I wish him the best."

00:09:42.581 --> 00:09:44.249
That would be like slipping
a note cut out

00:09:44.249 --> 00:09:46.152
from magazine letters
under his door that said,

00:09:46.152 --> 00:09:47.453
"I'm gonna murder you
in your sleep.

00:09:47.453 --> 00:09:49.155
Warmest regards,
your dear friend, Donald."

00:09:49.155 --> 00:09:50.288
[ Laughter ]

00:09:50.288 --> 00:09:52.091
Obviously, there's a lot
of bad blood there.

00:09:52.091 --> 00:09:54.126
But the best part is,
all these are awful guys.

00:09:54.126 --> 00:09:55.594
Bolton's an unrepentant
warmonger,

00:09:55.594 --> 00:09:56.728
and Trump, of course, is Trump,

00:09:56.728 --> 00:09:58.397
so it's fun to watch them
turn on each other

00:09:58.397 --> 00:09:59.598
and try to take each other down.

00:09:59.598 --> 00:10:02.134
I don't like watching
nature shows where a lion

00:10:02.134 --> 00:10:04.470
kills a baby antelope,
but when they show a spider

00:10:04.470 --> 00:10:06.605
and a scorpion going at it,
I am in.

00:10:06.605 --> 00:10:08.674
[ Laughter ]

00:10:08.674 --> 00:10:11.009
So the actual facts of
what happened are indefensible.

00:10:11.009 --> 00:10:13.946
There's nothing Republicans can
say to defend what Trump did.

00:10:13.946 --> 00:10:16.114
That's why they're focused
instead on the process.

00:10:16.114 --> 00:10:18.584
They've been whining for weeks
about how Democrats

00:10:18.584 --> 00:10:21.119
have been conducting the initial
depositions behind closed doors

00:10:21.119 --> 00:10:24.589
even though a lot of them
are allowed in those hearings.

00:10:24.589 --> 00:10:28.260
In fact, this week, CNN asked
Republican Congressman Ted Yoho

00:10:28.260 --> 00:10:30.729
if he had attended
any of the impeachment hearings.

00:10:30.729 --> 00:10:33.465
There was even a deposition
going on while he was on TV,

00:10:33.465 --> 00:10:35.334
and the anchor asked him
why he wasn't there.

00:10:35.334 --> 00:10:37.936
-You could attend
all of these depositions.

00:10:37.936 --> 00:10:40.106
Have you attended a single one?

00:10:40.106 --> 00:10:42.874
-No, I haven't gone to those.
-But why are you not there?

00:10:42.874 --> 00:10:46.044
-Because I have other
responsibilities in the House.

00:10:46.044 --> 00:10:48.380
-Respectfully, Congressman,
as glad as I am

00:10:48.380 --> 00:10:51.450
that you're on this show, you
don't need to be on this show.

00:10:51.450 --> 00:10:52.985
You could be in there --
-Well, like I said --

00:10:52.985 --> 00:10:55.888
-You could be in there
deposing --

00:10:55.888 --> 00:10:57.022
-I plan to go in there.

00:10:57.022 --> 00:10:58.757
I've got my questions
written for him.

00:10:58.757 --> 00:11:00.692
-So you are going
to this deposition

00:11:00.692 --> 00:11:01.961
after you're off the air
with us.

00:11:01.961 --> 00:11:03.162
Is that right?
-As soon as I'm off the air.

00:11:03.162 --> 00:11:04.196
Yes, ma'am.

00:11:04.196 --> 00:11:06.065
-No, I don't think so.
[ Laughter ]

00:11:06.065 --> 00:11:08.401
I mean, based on that,
I bet he didn't actually

00:11:08.401 --> 00:11:09.769
have any questions written down.

00:11:09.769 --> 00:11:11.269
"I got my questions right here."

00:11:11.269 --> 00:11:12.671
"Okay.
Can you read some of them?"

00:11:12.671 --> 00:11:14.607
"Yeah.
Y-You bet."

00:11:14.607 --> 00:11:16.642
[ Light laughter ]

00:11:19.879 --> 00:11:26.718
[ Laughter ]

00:11:26.718 --> 00:11:28.020
"I don't have any questions."

00:11:28.020 --> 00:11:29.788
[ Laughter ]

00:11:29.788 --> 00:11:31.891
Today was a historic day
and a major step forward

00:11:31.891 --> 00:11:33.058
in the impeachment process.

00:11:33.058 --> 00:11:35.227
Republicans can't defend Trump
on the substance

00:11:35.227 --> 00:11:36.828
and they can't complain
about the process,

00:11:36.828 --> 00:11:38.430
so now all they have left is...

00:11:38.430 --> 00:11:39.698
-Bull [bleep]

00:11:39.698 --> 00:11:41.367
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:11:41.367 --> 00:11:44.770
[ Cheers and applause ]

